[h1]build84 - loot volume trimmed, and the orbs stop guaranteeing legendaries[/h1]

A database-only update. No map, quest or text change, so an existing character is unaffected and no
new game is needed.

[h2]What changed[/h2]

Two things Will asked for after playing build83.

[b]1. The canonical chests and orbs pay a run's worth of loot, not a vendor's stock.[/b]
The two Polis Vault gaoler cage chests were dropping roughly 36 legendary-grade pieces between them on a
single run. That is now trimmed hard across 69 canonical loot surfaces: the two-chest cage run stays under
about 4 to 5 pieces on Normal and Legendary and around 3 on Epic, and it still guarantees at least one
piece at the target grade on at least 95 percent of runs. The boss and guard hoards, the level-banded uber
orbs and Charon's orb are trimmed the same way. Only the spawn count of each table moved; nothing was added
to, or removed from, any loot pool.

[b]2. Mystical Orbs no longer guarantee a legendary.[/b]
The three apex orb tables carried a reward row that fired on every open and could pay a legendary. That row
is demoted from a 100 percent chance to the same 21.2 percent the rest of the orb family already uses. The
worst orb now pays about 0.85 legendary items per open instead of 8.4, so a legendary out of an orb is a
treat again rather than a certainty. A legendary is still possible at a real rate, so the orbs are not
turned into empty boxes.

[h2]The local testing farm is untouched[/h2]

The trim applies to the shipped game only. The heavier local playtest chests keep their old volume through
a separate copy that exists purely for testing and can never be reached in the shipped map.

[h2]One honest note[/h2]

A legendary is now less than guaranteed but not yet genuinely rare: the best orbs still turn one up on
roughly six opens in ten. Tightening that further changes the reward mix, so it is being left for a
separate, deliberate decision rather than slipped into this update.

[h2]Verification[/h2]

Built twice from the committed source with byte-identical output. The change modifies 69 loot tables and
adds 44 records used only by the local testing map. The shipped map, quests, text and creatures are
byte-for-byte identical to build83. Every existing gate still passes, including loot distribution, orb and
chest breadth, craft and thrown, relic tiers and the Immortal Throne campaign cap, and the contract suite
adds zero new blocking issues over the previous release.
